{
  "task": "T1701",
  "status": "Focused parsed-source and serialized-bytecode owner controls pass; shared full library and ordinary/native acceptance remain pending",
  "tested_commit": "7e4e81f81a1d24319ee282aa8dfd63578cfb4db7",
  "baseline_commit": "1f14386f0e46ea52d29ddaeec04ff5eeb58e6ac0",
  "base_commit": "d0d51e262d97f93cbdda9d1e45084ef8c290594a",
  "root_cause": "Width-only method mangling merged USize with UInt64 and ISize/Int64 with Int before preserving their source declarations. Qualified alias calls then lost the same owner at interpreter width normalization. Declarations with equal carriers can have distinct result contracts.",
  "repair": "Codegen first resolves aliases and current source mounts and selects an exact registered numeric method of the right arity. Runtime gives an exact declared numeric body precedence before width normalization, using its self parameter and shared nested-call path. PTR is eligibility for the existing pointer-sized scalar carrier, not owner identity. By-value CBGR receivers stay on the existing outer unwrap path; declared reference methods retain their reference.",
  "controls": [
    "Static, instance, cast and alias calls distinguish USize/ISize List-returning bodies from UInt64/Int64 fixed-array bodies.",
    "Bodies use distinct source marker values, and every test executes direct and serialized/deserialized VBC. Independent free functions validate the fixed-array and List carriers.",
    "Signed alias chains and parenthesized receivers, reversed implementation order, Float32/Float64 result widths, borrowed-by-value receivers and declared reference receivers preserve the chosen body.",
    "A separately declared record named USize has a nonnumeric TypeId and cannot capture the builtin numeric dispatch. The retained log prints its actual body/self descriptor."
  ],
