  "interpretation": [
    "The isolated baseline has 2 passes and 5 failures. Static calls and independent carrier controls pass while instance/cast/alias owner selection fails.",
    "The first owner repair has 3 passes and 4 failures because pointer-sized integers share TypeId::PTR, which is not is_numeric(). Adding that existing carrier as eligibility yields 7 passes.",
    "The expanded adjacent gate has 11 passes and 2 failures, but only its borrowed-by-value failure is a valid new production oracle. Its original supposed foreign fixture placed implement USize inside a module without declaring a foreign USize; that still names the builtin and was an invalid refusal expectation.",
    "The exact-name/CBGR follow-up yields 13 passes and the same invalid fixture failure. Declaring a separate record corrects the fixture; the final gate passes all 14 controls with zero ignores.",
    "The exact-name runtime guard is source-reviewed defensive narrowing. The corrected negative emits a bare USize.to_be_bytes descriptor with record TypeId19; it proves the numeric-self eligibility refusal, not a qualified suffix lookup branch."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "These tests parse source directly into VBC. They do not run the typechecker, load a fresh standard-library archive, or certify the ordinary CLI, registry, AOT, or all imported method aliases.",
    "The inherited stage14 precompiled artifacts remain byte-identical. No automatic producer bake was run.",
    "The marker bodies isolate owner selection from endian conversion and callable array-to-List materialization. Those producer/storage boundaries are tested separately under T1698, T1700 and T1704.",
    "The full required VBC library gate is intentionally reserved for one coherent integrated candidate. The task remains open until its ordinary/native acceptance is established.",
    "Earlier harness compile failures and the stopped cold checker-target attempt establish no production acceptance; the isolated executable baseline is the first acceptance baseline used here."
